--- a/.andromeda/security-plan.md
+++ b/.andromeda/security-plan.md
@@ -9,4 +9,4 @@
 decision/cargo-deny-gate · Cargo deny gate on the root graph — Cargo dependencies are held to cargo deny check over the root lockfile: advisories, licences, sources and C-crate, telemetry-crate and feature bans. · guard: cargo deny check · except: the test-only fuzz workspace sits outside it by a ratified exemption, its lockfile getting its own advisory and source audit
-decision/child-output-tolerant · Child output parsed tolerantly — Output of spawned children is parsed tolerantly and a failure becomes unknown.
-decision/child-output-tolerant-unknown · Child output parsing fails to unknown — Child output parsing is tolerant, and a failure becomes unknown.
+decision/child-output-tolerant · Child output parsed tolerantly — Output of spawned children is parsed tolerantly, and a failure becomes unknown or a closed failure word.
+decision/child-output-tolerant-unknown · Child output parsing fails to unknown — Child output parsing is tolerant, and a failure becomes unknown or a closed failure word.
 decision/child-path-trust · Child processes trust PATH — Spawned child processes are whatever the calling process's PATH resolves to.
@@ -235,2 +235,3 @@
 decision/hooks-fail-open · Hooks fail open — Every hook failure fails open: exit 0 with no body.
+decision/hyprctl-read-deadline · hyprctl child bounded by a deadline — The hyprctl child runs with null stdin and the named environment variables removed, under a 5 s deadline at which it is killed and reaped; a deadline kill or a non-zero exit reads as unreachable. · guard: read_past_the_deadline_kills_and_reaps_its_child · provisional
 decision/input-box-readiness-from-literals · Input box readiness read from compiled literals — The input box reads up only on compiled literals, a footer literal or a rule row of at least 40 rule chars directly above a row opening the prompt char, and never while a modal literal stands; one predicate decides for verify and for viola run's pre-send gate. · why: A boundary widening that was ratified.
@@ -253,3 +254,3 @@
 decision/no-width-or-colour-override-env · No width or colour override env — COLUMNS, CLICOLOR, CLICOLOR_FORCE and CI are not read; the board's width comes from the host terminal size, no env read.
-decision/parser-fuzz-scope · Parser surfaces in fuzz scope — Paste text validation, channel ndjson framing, the hook stdin parser, the claude agents output parser and the vt100 feed are in scope for fuzz and property coverage.
+decision/parser-fuzz-scope · Parser surfaces in fuzz scope — Paste text validation, channel ndjson framing, the hook stdin parser, the claude agents output parser, the hyprctl reply parsers and the vt100 feed are in scope for fuzz and property coverage.
 decision/paste-text-character-set · Paste text character set — Paste text allows LF, CR and TAB and refuses every other C0 control, DEL and every C1 character, checked over decoded characters.
@@ -271,3 +272,3 @@
 decision/session-id-argv-no-shell · Session id as one argv element — The session id after --resume has the closed session-id shape and is one argv element of a direct spawn, never passed through a shell.
-decision/shared-validators-in-core · Shared validators in the core crate — Input validators live in viola-core and every surface (CLI, MCP, wrapper) calls the same one. · why: so the CLI, MCP and the wrapper apply one identical check
+decision/shared-validators-in-core · Shared validators in the core crate — Input validators live in viola-core and every surface (CLI, MCP, wrapper) calls the same one. · why: so the CLI, MCP and the wrapper apply one identical check · except: The Hyprland seam's window Address validator lives in the seam crate.
 decision/single-shell-out · statusline_command is the only shell-out — The recorded command runs only from hook statusline, as /bin/sh -c with the command as one argument, its stdout capped and never parsed, its wait bounded; it is the only shell-out, and a second one is never added.
@@ -363,2 +364,4 @@
 decision/fixtures-reviewed-before-commit · Fixtures reviewed before commit — Recorded fixture payloads are reviewed for home paths, usernames and tool input before committing.
+decision/hyprland-recorder-string-allowlist · Hyprland recorder keeps strings by a closed allowlist — viola-hypr-tap keeps a reply string only under a closed per-request key allowlist in the form the seam parses (window addresses, the v-digit version tag); every other string becomes the placeholder, a non-JSON reply stays only as ok, then the shared scrub runs and an unclean set is refused whole. · why: Hyprland 0.56.2 carries titles and user text under keys no deny-list foresees (lastwindowtitle, nested workspace.name, tags). · guard: record_replaces_every_string_off_the_allowlist; planted_hyprland_lastwindowtitle_is_rejected
+decision/hyprland-reply-text-dropped · Hyprland reply text dropped at the parse — Hyprland reply types hold no text field: window titles, classes and every other reply string are dropped at the parse and reach no log line and no error. · guard: contract_hyprland_canary_reaches_no_line_and_no_error
 decision/link-names-kept-out-of-process-log · Link names kept out of the process log — The wrapper's link and unlink methods write no process-log line of their own and their request and response lines carry no name; viola link and unlink print only their own parsed arguments, never a name read back from a reply or log.
